1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,367
<i> Why are they here?</i>

2
00:00:01,533 --> 00:00:02,067
<i>This is the only thing
I can do...</i>

3
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:03,233
<i> to protect all of you.</i>

4
00:00:03,367 --> 00:00:06,133
<i>The syndicate is doing
everything to find you.</i>

5
00:00:06,267 --> 00:00:08,767
<i>Where are you hiding now, Joey.</i>

6
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:09,900
<i> Are you okay, Hon?</i>

7
00:00:10,033 --> 00:00:11,600
<i> You seem affected by the news.</i>

8
00:00:11,733 --> 00:00:13,167
<i> Don't talk like that.</i>

9
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:16,200
<i>I trusted you
and you betrayed me?</i>

10
00:00:16,333 --> 00:00:17,967
<i>You know that your life
is in danger.</i>

11
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:19,467
<i>We need to get rid of the pests</i>

12
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:20,733
<i> in our organization.</i>

13
00:00:20,867 --> 00:00:22,767
<i> Jin Ho, what are you doing?</i>

14
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:23,767
<i> I got thirsty.</i>

15
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:24,700
<i> I'll cook.</i>

16
00:00:24,833 --> 00:00:26,233
<i>I'll be the one
to prepare lunch.</i>

17
00:00:26,367 --> 00:00:28,700
<i>- I'll do it.
- This is what I want.</i>

18
00:00:28,833 --> 00:00:30,267
<i>Thank you,
because you thought of me</i>

19
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:31,400
<i> when I wasn't feeling well.</i>

20
00:00:31,533 --> 00:00:32,400
<i> Wait here.</i>

21
00:00:32,533 --> 00:00:33,900
<i> I'll just talk to these three.</i>

22
00:00:34,067 --> 00:00:35,467
<i> Follow me!</i>

23
00:00:37,333 --> 00:00:39,600
<i> [OBB]</i>

24
00:00:53,467 --> 00:00:55,267
What? You think I did not notice

25
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:57,233
that you're making moves
on my daughter?

26
00:00:57,367 --> 00:00:58,733
[LIGHT PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

27
00:00:58,867 --> 00:01:00,667
You're even sucking up to me!

28
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:02,067
Sorry, Sir.

29
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:03,567
Don't play dumb!

30
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:04,967
I know you understand me!

31
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:05,967
Uncle Miguel,

32
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:08,733
you're angry with me too?

33
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:10,733
Joey isn't feeling well,

34
00:01:10,867 --> 00:01:12,167
I'm just trying to cheer her up.

35
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:13,400
Your style is rotten!

36
00:01:13,533 --> 00:01:15,333
You're just starting,
I've already been there.

37
00:01:15,467 --> 00:01:17,133
Ah, because you used to do that,
Uncle...

38
00:01:17,267 --> 00:01:19,700
Ah, Major, you used to do that?

39
00:01:19,833 --> 00:01:22,233
Yes, but I stay in my lane.

40
00:01:22,367 --> 00:01:23,433
You might be forgetting.

41
00:01:23,567 --> 00:01:27,000
We're here hiding
from the syndicate.

42
00:01:27,133 --> 00:01:28,900
Behave yourselves, okay?

43
00:01:29,033 --> 00:01:33,400
[LIGHT PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

44
00:01:34,867 --> 00:01:36,500
I'm on my way.

45
00:01:37,367 --> 00:01:40,000
Just make sure
nothing happens to me.

46
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:42,833
Please guarantee my protection.
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

47
00:01:42,967 --> 00:01:44,900
<i>Don't worry, Liza,
I will take care of you.</i>

48
00:01:45,033 --> 00:01:48,067
<i>Chief is trying to call
Major Delgado.</i>

49
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:50,400
<i>It would be better
if we meet now.</i>

50
00:01:50,533 --> 00:01:52,433
<i> I'm leaving now.</i>

51
00:01:52,567 --> 00:01:56,600
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

52
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,133
What's your problem?

53
00:02:21,267 --> 00:02:22,767
You're ruining my plan!

54
00:02:22,900 --> 00:02:25,767
Well, I'm just trying
to patch things up with Joey.

55
00:02:25,900 --> 00:02:27,067
I hurt her.

56
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:29,500
Now, I'm trying
to make it up to her.

57
00:02:29,633 --> 00:02:31,033
You guys!
No take backs!

58
00:02:31,167 --> 00:02:32,433
You let your chance pass!

59
00:02:32,567 --> 00:02:33,300
He's right!

60
00:02:33,433 --> 00:02:34,867
You should give chance
to others.

61
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:36,500
- [CHUCKLES]
- Give chance to others?

62
00:02:36,633 --> 00:02:38,833
You too? I thought
there was a bro code?

63
00:02:38,967 --> 00:02:40,167
What happened to that?
[LIGHT PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

64
00:02:40,300 --> 00:02:41,667
Like you?

65
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:43,133
You know what?

66
00:02:43,267 --> 00:02:47,133
All is fair in love and war.

67
00:02:48,667 --> 00:02:50,733
Ah, so that's it...

68
00:02:50,867 --> 00:02:51,733
you want war...

69
00:02:51,867 --> 00:02:53,100
Okay, I am in!

70
00:02:53,233 --> 00:02:54,267
Oh, come on!

71
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:55,400
Love and war, huh.

72
00:02:55,533 --> 00:02:56,667
If that's the case,
then I am in!

73
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:58,967
- Oh, come on!
- [SPLASHES]

74
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:00,667
You guys need to cool down, huh!

75
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:02,767
You're a traitor, Oppa!
What?

76
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:04,533
Survival of the fittest, huh!

77
00:03:04,667 --> 00:03:05,667
You think so.

78
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:07,267
[GROWLS]

79
00:03:09,333 --> 00:03:12,500
Dad, will they be okay there?

80
00:03:12,633 --> 00:03:13,700
Let them be.

81
00:03:13,833 --> 00:03:15,533
They look like they're enjoying.

82
00:03:16,733 --> 00:03:18,067
- [GRUNTING]
- Hey, hey!

83
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:19,733
Hey, can you stop?

84
00:03:19,867 --> 00:03:21,000
Can you stop?
Can you stop, please?

85
00:03:21,167 --> 00:03:22,700
- Enough!
- [GRUNTING]

86
00:03:24,433 --> 00:03:25,367
Come on.

87
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:26,833
It's cold.

88
00:03:26,967 --> 00:03:28,433
You should rest.

89
00:03:28,567 --> 00:03:31,267
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

90
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:32,800
What happened there?

91
00:03:32,933 --> 00:03:34,467
Ah, ignore them.

92
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:35,933
- Let's just talk!
- Oppa!

93
00:03:36,067 --> 00:03:37,733
Come on, come on, come on!

94
00:03:37,867 --> 00:03:38,833
Come on!

95
00:03:38,967 --> 00:03:41,533
- [YELPS]
- [SPLASHES]

96
00:03:41,667 --> 00:03:45,333
[CAR HORN BLARING]

97
00:03:45,467 --> 00:03:49,500
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

98
00:03:58,833 --> 00:04:01,200
You're blocking my way.

99
00:04:01,333 --> 00:04:03,067
Where are you going again?

100
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:05,600
None of your business.

101
00:04:05,733 --> 00:04:09,433
I didn't get any memo to ask
permission from you, did I?

102
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:11,900
[GRUNTS]

103
00:04:12,433 --> 00:04:13,400
[SPITS]

104
00:04:13,533 --> 00:04:15,100
- What's wrong with you?
- Oh, enough, enough!

105
00:04:15,233 --> 00:04:16,433
[SPLASHING]

106
00:04:16,567 --> 00:04:17,767
Enough! I surrender!

107
00:04:17,900 --> 00:04:18,733
I surrender.

108
00:04:18,867 --> 00:04:19,900
You surrender, so...

109
00:04:20,033 --> 00:04:21,033
Okay, I win.

110
00:04:21,167 --> 00:04:22,433
What?
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

111
00:04:22,567 --> 00:04:24,233
You said you surrender.

112
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,000
[CHUCKLES]

113
00:04:26,133 --> 00:04:27,433
You wish.

114
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:29,367
What do you mean you wish?
What's your problem?

115
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:31,533
You already have Liza, right?

116
00:04:31,933 --> 00:04:32,800
Why are you interfering?

117
00:04:32,933 --> 00:04:34,000
Exactly!

118
00:04:44,300 --> 00:04:45,600
Yes, you're just hurting Joey!

119
00:04:45,733 --> 00:04:47,067
That's true!

120
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:48,600
Okay, that was then.

121
00:04:48,733 --> 00:04:51,400
Okay? I admit I hurt her.

122
00:04:51,533 --> 00:04:53,367
But now, I'm fixing it,

123
00:04:53,500 --> 00:04:55,267
and I'm trying to make it work.

124
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:56,300
Okay?

125
00:04:56,433 --> 00:04:57,933
- Wait, why you?
- What?

126
00:04:58,067 --> 00:04:59,433
I'm Joey's friend,

127
00:04:59,567 --> 00:05:01,433
so I have the biggest chance.

128
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:03,267
Right, you're her friend.

129
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:05,667
You're her friend,
and then what?

130
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:08,000
Your face is back on TV again.

131
00:05:08,133 --> 00:05:09,000
Do you know that?

132
00:05:09,133 --> 00:05:11,633
That means if someone sees you,

133
00:05:11,767 --> 00:05:13,333
it's another problem!

134
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:15,467
Fine!

135
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:17,033
If you don't want me to go out,

136
00:05:17,167 --> 00:05:19,100
you buy what I need.

137
00:05:23,167 --> 00:05:26,900
I need wet wipes, napkin,
and feminine wash,

138
00:05:27,033 --> 00:05:28,500
and I need it now.

139
00:05:28,633 --> 00:05:30,867
You should also park my car,
okay?

140
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:35,133
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

141
00:05:48,933 --> 00:05:49,967
Okay, guys.
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

142
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:50,933
- Oh, fine.
- Okay?

143
00:05:51,067 --> 00:05:52,667
Gentleman's agreement, okay?

144
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:55,133
Whoever Joey chooses,
that's final!

145
00:05:55,267 --> 00:05:56,500
No one else meddle.

146
00:05:56,633 --> 00:05:57,900
If she chooses me,
don't intrude.

147
00:05:58,033 --> 00:06:00,367
Okay, fine!
Fine! Fine!

148
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:02,400
[SPLASHING]

149
00:06:02,533 --> 00:06:03,967
You're so annoying.

150
00:06:04,767 --> 00:06:06,167
Hey!

151
00:06:09,367 --> 00:06:10,467
You know, Joey...

152
00:06:11,067 --> 00:06:13,200
I have this fear

153
00:06:13,333 --> 00:06:15,067
that I'll lose you someday.

154
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:16,867
Dad, why?

155
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:18,933
Do we have enemies here?

156
00:06:19,067 --> 00:06:20,567
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

157
00:06:20,700 --> 00:06:22,167
Yes.

158
00:06:22,933 --> 00:06:24,733
Those three eggs.

159
00:06:26,900 --> 00:06:28,600
They are my enemies.

160
00:06:28,733 --> 00:06:30,667
Joey, I know...

161
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:32,967
the day will come...

162
00:06:34,233 --> 00:06:36,667
you'll be separated
from me and your mother.

163
00:06:37,267 --> 00:06:40,333
You'll find someone you love.

164
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:44,133
You'll have your own family.

165
00:06:44,300 --> 00:06:49,900
You know, no matter
how much I prepare.

166
00:06:50,033 --> 00:06:53,033
When that day comes, surely...

167
00:06:53,933 --> 00:06:55,900
surely, I'll be hurt.

168
00:06:56,033 --> 00:06:57,733
Dad, where did that come from?

169
00:06:57,867 --> 00:07:01,367
Why are you suddenly
saying that?

170
00:07:02,233 --> 00:07:03,367
Ah, someone...

171
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:05,700
Someone reminded me...

172
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:08,767
I know that day will come.

173
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:11,867
Dad, that's still
a long time away, okay?

174
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,033
I know it's a long time away,

175
00:07:13,167 --> 00:07:14,433
but that day will come.

176
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:17,067
And I hope
when that day comes...

177
00:07:17,733 --> 00:07:22,400
you'll find the man who will
love and care for you.

178
00:07:24,533 --> 00:07:26,633
That's me, I know.

179
00:07:28,167 --> 00:07:30,700
Like what you did for mom.

180
00:07:31,500 --> 00:07:33,033
That's why I think

181
00:07:33,167 --> 00:07:36,500
when I find a man for me,

182
00:07:36,900 --> 00:07:39,333
of course, I want
someone like you, loving,

183
00:07:39,467 --> 00:07:40,700
brave...

184
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:47,167
resourceful, clever.

185
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:48,300
That's me too.

186
00:07:48,467 --> 00:07:50,067
That's me too, I know.

187
00:07:51,867 --> 00:07:53,600
and principled.

188
00:07:56,867 --> 00:07:57,867
But it's hard to find someone

189
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:59,333
like you, Dad.

190
00:07:59,467 --> 00:08:00,333
So, what now?

191
00:08:00,467 --> 00:08:02,400
I think you'll have
a hard time too.

192
00:08:02,533 --> 00:08:03,833
So good luck to you.

193
00:08:03,967 --> 00:08:05,700
[CHUCKLES]

194
00:08:05,833 --> 00:08:07,267
But you know, Joey...

195
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:11,767
I hope you'll be happy.

196
00:08:11,900 --> 00:08:13,700
And remember,

197
00:08:13,833 --> 00:08:15,267
your mother and I are here

198
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:17,000
whenever you need us.

199
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:19,733
I'll make sure, Dad,

200
00:08:19,867 --> 00:08:21,933
that I'll choose the right man,

201
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:24,067
and you'll be happy for me.

202
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:26,700
I want someone...

203
00:08:26,833 --> 00:08:30,000
as loving as you
and as handsome.

204
00:08:30,633 --> 00:08:31,833
There, you'll have
a hard time there.

205
00:08:31,967 --> 00:08:34,233
Yes! Love you!

206
00:08:34,367 --> 00:08:38,533
[PLEASANT MUSIC CONTINUES]

207
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:45,067
It's one of us three.

208
00:08:47,433 --> 00:08:48,467
Hey!

209
00:08:48,600 --> 00:08:49,933
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

210
00:08:50,067 --> 00:08:51,200
What are you doing here?

211
00:08:51,333 --> 00:08:53,433
Ah, looking for eggs.

212
00:08:53,567 --> 00:08:55,433
Ah, nothing.
Ah, we're cleaning.

213
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:56,767
Good night, good night!
Good night, Joey!

214
00:08:56,900 --> 00:08:58,867
Good night! Good night!

215
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:02,900
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

216
00:09:04,767 --> 00:09:06,500
Go rest now, Joey.

217
00:09:07,133 --> 00:09:08,067
Good night, Dad.
I love you.

218
00:09:08,200 --> 00:09:09,500
Love you.

219
00:09:12,233 --> 00:09:14,400
What? You woke up early.

220
00:09:14,533 --> 00:09:16,067
They woke up earlier.

221
00:09:16,933 --> 00:09:17,967
Huh?

222
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:19,467
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

223
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:20,567
Wow, wow...

224
00:09:20,700 --> 00:09:22,600
Okay, just relax.

225
00:09:23,033 --> 00:09:24,300
You can do it.

226
00:09:25,033 --> 00:09:25,900
- Oh...
- Oh.

227
00:09:26,033 --> 00:09:27,767
Release the brake a little.

228
00:09:27,933 --> 00:09:28,967
- There, there.
- Okay, there.

229
00:09:29,100 --> 00:09:30,667
- Whoo!
- There, there, okay.

230
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:33,267
- Don't let go.
- I won't let go.

231
00:09:34,800 --> 00:09:36,567
See, I can do it.

232
00:09:38,033 --> 00:09:39,333
- Oh, oh, oh, oh...
- Hey, hey, hey, hey!

233
00:09:39,467 --> 00:09:40,800
I might fall!

234
00:09:40,933 --> 00:09:41,733
No, no, no, no!

235
00:09:41,867 --> 00:09:43,433
Ouch! Whoo...

236
00:09:43,567 --> 00:09:44,500
Sorry.

237
00:09:44,633 --> 00:09:45,500
I got nervous.

238
00:09:45,633 --> 00:09:47,700
But in fairness, I can do it.

239
00:09:47,833 --> 00:09:48,800
Yes.

240
00:09:48,933 --> 00:09:50,033
Wait, ah...

241
00:09:50,167 --> 00:09:51,267
Are you okay?

242
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:53,067
I'm okay.

243
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:54,933
- Good thing...
- I have something to say.

244
00:09:55,067 --> 00:09:57,000
Oh, you have something to say?

245
00:09:57,567 --> 00:10:00,233
Ah, you, you go first.

246
00:10:00,367 --> 00:10:02,733
Ah, I just want to say...

247
00:10:02,900 --> 00:10:05,067
Good thing we're okay now.

248
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:08,033
Actually, I thought about
what you said.

249
00:10:08,167 --> 00:10:09,333
It's true.

250
00:10:09,467 --> 00:10:11,367
We're not really meant
for each other.

251
00:10:11,500 --> 00:10:14,200
Because you're such
a serious person.

252
00:10:14,333 --> 00:10:17,800
I don't even know
if you can smile.

253
00:10:18,333 --> 00:10:19,900
You're mature already.

254
00:10:21,967 --> 00:10:23,900
Old, like that?

255
00:10:24,033 --> 00:10:25,467
Not really, I mean...

256
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:28,467
Because me, I still have a lot
to experience

257
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:29,900
and want to do.
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

258
00:10:30,033 --> 00:10:31,400
I don't even know
how to ride a bike.

259
00:10:31,533 --> 00:10:33,300
That's why I'll teach you.

260
00:10:34,133 --> 00:10:36,367
I'll teach you like...

261
00:10:36,533 --> 00:10:37,900
This, biking.

262
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:44,200
Because...

263
00:10:44,333 --> 00:10:45,200
that's how it is, right?

264
00:10:45,333 --> 00:10:47,933
When you're friends,
you help each other.

265
00:10:49,700 --> 00:10:52,967
That's why I hope
we can help Jin Ho too.

266
00:10:53,933 --> 00:10:55,233
For me, that's what I want,

267
00:10:55,367 --> 00:10:56,833
that no matter what happens,

268
00:10:56,967 --> 00:11:00,267
the four of us will
still have a solid friendship.

269
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:06,100
Okay.

270
00:11:06,233 --> 00:11:07,633
Ah...

271
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:10,000
You also had something to say,
right?

272
00:11:10,400 --> 00:11:11,800
Ah...

273
00:11:12,800 --> 00:11:14,067
Nothing.

274
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:15,467
- Nothing.
- Are you sure?

275
00:11:15,600 --> 00:11:17,967
Yes, come on,
let's go biking.

276
00:11:18,767 --> 00:11:20,033
Okay.

277
00:11:24,267 --> 00:11:25,967
- Hey!
- Slowly.

278
00:11:26,100 --> 00:11:27,800
Hey!

279
00:11:28,467 --> 00:11:31,300
Had I known,
I would've woken up earlier.

280
00:11:32,300 --> 00:11:33,767
[SIGHS]

281
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:36,600
Early bird gets the worm,
really.

282
00:11:36,733 --> 00:11:39,667
But the second mouse
gets the cheese.

283
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,067
What? What does that mean?
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

284
00:11:45,433 --> 00:11:46,567
We'll see.

285
00:11:46,700 --> 00:11:49,467
Hey...

286
00:11:51,467 --> 00:11:52,333
Let's do it again next time.

287
00:11:52,467 --> 00:11:54,633
So, was biking okay, Joey?

288
00:11:54,767 --> 00:11:57,100
Oh, honestly, I still felt
a bit awkward.

289
00:11:57,233 --> 00:11:58,567
A little more practice.

290
00:11:58,700 --> 00:12:01,267
But the one teaching me
is really good.

291
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:02,800
Yes.

292
00:12:05,733 --> 00:12:06,600
That's right.

293
00:12:06,733 --> 00:12:07,967
Oh, were you saying something?

294
00:12:13,533 --> 00:12:14,633
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]
Ah, yes.

295
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:16,867
Actually, once I learn
how to bike,

296
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,367
maybe he can teach me to ride a
motorcycle!

297
00:12:19,500 --> 00:12:21,433
- What?
- Yes.

298
00:12:21,567 --> 00:12:23,933
Okay, I'll return this now.

299
00:12:24,767 --> 00:12:26,367
- Can you do it?
- I can now.

300
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:28,133
You're old.

301
00:12:32,067 --> 00:12:33,967
- Hey.
- Oh!

302
00:12:34,100 --> 00:12:36,300
- Snake! Snake!
- Where? Where?

303
00:12:36,433 --> 00:12:37,767
- Where? Where?
- Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

304
00:12:37,900 --> 00:12:39,667
[CHUCKLES]

305
00:12:42,767 --> 00:12:44,167
- Whoa!
- Hey!

306
00:12:44,300 --> 00:12:45,333
- That got me.
- Why us?

307
00:12:45,467 --> 00:12:47,267
He's mad, look.

308
00:12:48,233 --> 00:12:49,767
Prank lang 'yun!

309
00:12:49,900 --> 00:12:50,967
- Prank...
- OA.

310
00:12:51,100 --> 00:12:52,800
I am just kidding.

311
00:12:52,933 --> 00:12:54,333
Goodbye!

312
00:12:55,467 --> 00:12:56,333
Take care!

313
00:12:56,467 --> 00:12:58,267
[JOEY CHUCKLES]

314
00:12:58,400 --> 00:12:59,400
Hey, say sorry!

315
00:12:59,533 --> 00:13:01,500
- Say sorry.
- Say sorry!

316
00:13:03,433 --> 00:13:06,433
[PLEASANT MUSIC CONTINUES]

317
00:13:08,233 --> 00:13:10,933
This is where we'll bond!

318
00:13:12,033 --> 00:13:13,967
Jin Ho, Peter!

319
00:13:14,100 --> 00:13:15,633
Come on, hurry!

320
00:13:15,767 --> 00:13:17,567
- Joey!
- Hey!

321
00:13:17,700 --> 00:13:19,833
- Hey!
- Amazing!

322
00:13:20,633 --> 00:13:21,933
What a nice place!

323
00:13:22,100 --> 00:13:25,033
Wow, Joey's really good
at finding spots.

324
00:13:25,167 --> 00:13:26,667
No, it's me.

325
00:13:26,800 --> 00:13:29,300
Come on, I just found
a nice spot,

326
00:13:29,433 --> 00:13:30,733
- you're overdoing the praise.
- Yes!

327
00:13:30,867 --> 00:13:33,367
[PETER SNIFFING]

328
00:13:33,500 --> 00:13:34,600
- Wow...
- Let's eat.

329
00:13:34,733 --> 00:13:35,967
- Right now?
- Yes.

330
00:13:36,100 --> 00:13:37,167
Do you want?

331
00:13:37,300 --> 00:13:38,267
No, I'll wait for the drinks.

332
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:40,000
Ah, drinks.

333
00:13:40,133 --> 00:13:41,600
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

334
00:13:41,733 --> 00:13:43,267
- For you.
- For me?

335
00:13:43,767 --> 00:13:45,533
Thank you.
It's delicious.

336
00:13:47,533 --> 00:13:50,100
-So, are you going to the beach?
- Ah, let's eat.

337
00:13:50,567 --> 00:13:51,767
Guys, guys, oh!

338
00:13:51,900 --> 00:13:53,367
- This is for you.
- There!

339
00:13:53,500 --> 00:13:54,667
It's really for you.

340
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:56,467
Actually, two for you.

341
00:13:57,400 --> 00:13:59,633
- Yes. That's so nice.
- It's destiny.

342
00:13:59,767 --> 00:14:02,000
- Very nice, thank you.
- We're, you know, friends.

343
00:14:02,133 --> 00:14:03,233
Thank you.

344
00:14:03,367 --> 00:14:04,833
- Thank you, Brother.
- Yes.

345
00:14:04,967 --> 00:14:06,667
Guys, you have two, okay.

346
00:14:06,800 --> 00:14:07,867
Enjoy!

347
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,700
For us, just one.

348
00:14:10,900 --> 00:14:12,400
- Oh, thank you.
- Joey.

349
00:14:12,533 --> 00:14:15,833
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

350
00:14:17,967 --> 00:14:20,067
You know, we should
all be careful here.

351
00:14:20,533 --> 00:14:23,200
There might be, you know,
insects like...

352
00:14:23,767 --> 00:14:25,333
Scary insects like...

353
00:14:25,467 --> 00:14:28,167
- Maybe bees, right?
- Ah...

354
00:14:28,333 --> 00:14:31,867
And, you know,
like wild animals, right.

355
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:33,100
Like...

356
00:14:33,233 --> 00:14:34,833
Snake! Snake! Snake!

357
00:14:34,967 --> 00:14:39,067
[SCREAMING]

358
00:14:41,300 --> 00:14:43,567
Oh, so you're good
at pranks too.

359
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:45,000
What do you think of me?

360
00:14:45,133 --> 00:14:46,300
Old?

361
00:14:46,433 --> 00:14:48,133
- Ah, you're not?
- No.

362
00:14:49,067 --> 00:14:50,033
Oh, oh, oh.

363
00:14:50,167 --> 00:14:51,467
Don't get mad, okay?

364
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:53,667
You started it, right?

365
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:58,400
Okay, okay, we'll let you
off this time.

366
00:14:58,533 --> 00:15:00,067
- We're even now, okay?
- Okay, fine.

367
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:01,433
- We're even.
- Is this a snake?

368
00:15:01,600 --> 00:15:02,767
- What?
- Is this a snake?

369
00:15:02,900 --> 00:15:04,367
Yeah.
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

370
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:05,933
Yuck.

371
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:08,567
- Yuck.
- [CHUCKLES]

372
00:15:10,967 --> 00:15:12,900
- Here.
- You can do it!

373
00:15:13,033 --> 00:15:14,433
Ah...

374
00:15:14,567 --> 00:15:15,667
Snake, snake!

375
00:15:15,800 --> 00:15:16,733
Nice.

376
00:15:16,867 --> 00:15:18,100
- Snake.
- [CHUCKLES]

377
00:15:18,233 --> 00:15:19,567
Cheers!

378
00:15:20,100 --> 00:15:22,167
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

379
00:15:23,500 --> 00:15:24,400
Oh...

380
00:15:24,533 --> 00:15:25,800
What is that for?

381
00:15:27,333 --> 00:15:31,833
Well, of course, to celebrate
our friendship.

382
00:15:32,500 --> 00:15:33,600
I hope it's always like this,

383
00:15:33,733 --> 00:15:35,700
no problems.

384
00:15:36,933 --> 00:15:39,767
Yes, we all wish that.
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

385
00:15:39,900 --> 00:15:40,933
That's right.

386
00:15:41,067 --> 00:15:44,433
We don't really know
what will happen,

387
00:15:44,567 --> 00:15:46,233
especially to Jin Ho.

388
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:53,867
Oh, why do you all look sad
suddenly?

389
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:57,000
You know, whatever we're going
through,

390
00:15:57,600 --> 00:16:00,767
we should still think
of being happy.

391
00:16:00,900 --> 00:16:02,300
Like me now, I'm happy...

392
00:16:02,433 --> 00:16:06,167
because I'm with
the most handsome,

393
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,567
most hardworking,

394
00:16:10,100 --> 00:16:12,733
most intelligent,

395
00:16:13,433 --> 00:16:15,700
and cool friends.

396
00:16:15,833 --> 00:16:18,300
But you know, I'm really
grateful to you

397
00:16:18,433 --> 00:16:21,267
because whatever I tell you,

398
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:23,467
I feel safe.

399
00:16:23,600 --> 00:16:25,500
I can trust you.

400
00:16:25,633 --> 00:16:26,600
My boy friends.

401
00:16:26,733 --> 00:16:28,267
Oh!

402
00:16:29,300 --> 00:16:31,367
Me? Boyfriend?
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

403
00:16:31,767 --> 00:16:33,167
Boy friends.

404
00:16:33,300 --> 00:16:35,733
because you're all boys

405
00:16:35,867 --> 00:16:38,033
and you're all my friends.

406
00:16:38,167 --> 00:16:40,500
- Ah...
- Boy friends.

407
00:16:40,633 --> 00:16:42,633
Oh, do you get it?

408
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:45,500
- Friends...
- Okay.

409
00:16:45,633 --> 00:16:46,767
- Cheers?
- Cheers!

410
00:16:46,900 --> 00:16:48,700
To Joey's boy friends.

411
00:16:48,833 --> 00:16:52,967
[PLEASANT MUSIC CONTINUES]

412
00:16:54,167 --> 00:16:56,567
[CHUCKLING]

413
00:16:56,700 --> 00:16:58,233
Liza!

414
00:16:59,667 --> 00:17:03,933
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

415
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:11,233
[PHONE CHIMES]

416
00:17:17,500 --> 00:17:20,700
<i>If you help us, we'll help you.</i>

417
00:17:20,833 --> 00:17:22,400
<i> Come over later.</i>

418
00:17:22,533 --> 00:17:24,233
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

419
00:17:31,167 --> 00:17:32,933
What are you doing here?

420
00:17:33,067 --> 00:17:34,700
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

421
00:17:34,833 --> 00:17:36,633
I've been here for a while.

422
00:17:36,767 --> 00:17:38,900
I brought the new effects.

423
00:17:39,033 --> 00:17:41,267
I was also with
one of our suppliers.

424
00:17:41,400 --> 00:17:42,967
Where did you come from?

425
00:17:44,333 --> 00:17:46,200
There you go again.

426
00:17:47,333 --> 00:17:49,033
If you're really curious,

427
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:51,133
the evidence is in the bathroom,

428
00:17:51,267 --> 00:17:52,700
still red.

429
00:17:53,967 --> 00:17:56,267
Anyway, I'll go
to the supplier now.

430
00:17:56,667 --> 00:17:58,133
Move aside.

431
00:17:58,267 --> 00:18:01,533
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

432
00:18:11,900 --> 00:18:13,567
[PHONE RINGS]

433
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:17,167
Did the supplier arrive?

434
00:18:18,067 --> 00:18:19,733
<i> Yes, Berdugo.</i>

435
00:18:19,867 --> 00:18:21,733
But we have one problem.

436
00:18:23,133 --> 00:18:24,900
What is it this time?

437
00:18:25,033 --> 00:18:27,333
The one you asked me to watch

438
00:18:27,767 --> 00:18:29,467
seems to be planning something.

439
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:31,100
If she tries,

440
00:18:31,233 --> 00:18:33,400
I'll kill her myself.

441
00:18:34,800 --> 00:18:36,467
"Kill her?"

442
00:18:36,600 --> 00:18:38,100
What do you mean?

443
00:18:38,233 --> 00:18:42,267
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

444
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:44,200
You're going to kill someone?

445
00:18:45,633 --> 00:18:47,367
It was just an expression.

446
00:18:48,033 --> 00:18:50,533
To be honest, I just got pissed
at my man.

447
00:18:50,667 --> 00:18:54,067
What did she do this time
to merit murder?

448
00:18:54,900 --> 00:18:56,367
It doesn't matter.

449
00:18:56,833 --> 00:18:59,633
Tomas, be careful
with what you say.

450
00:19:00,333 --> 00:19:03,500
What if the kids
or other people hear you?

451
00:19:03,633 --> 00:19:05,200
What will they think?

452
00:19:05,333 --> 00:19:06,933
Can you just let it go?
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

453
00:19:07,800 --> 00:19:09,600
And don't you ever dictate

454
00:19:09,733 --> 00:19:11,900
how I should speak!

455
00:19:12,033 --> 00:19:16,133
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

456
00:19:26,967 --> 00:19:28,733
I hope you're right, Jin Ho.

457
00:19:29,167 --> 00:19:30,767
<i>What do you mean you are
changing your mind?</i>

458
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:34,533
<i>You don't want to stay
in this organization anymore?</i>

459
00:19:34,667 --> 00:19:36,567
<i> Yes, you heard me.</i>

460
00:19:36,700 --> 00:19:37,733
<i> I'm done, Liza.</i>

461
00:19:37,867 --> 00:19:39,500
<i> We said it before...</i>

462
00:19:39,633 --> 00:19:40,667
<i> we get enough money...</i>

463
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:42,900
<i>- then we disappear.
- Disappear?</i>

464
00:19:43,033 --> 00:19:45,200
<i> This is our life, Jin Ho.</i>

465
00:19:45,333 --> 00:19:47,200
<i>You can't just walk away
from that.</i>

466
00:19:47,900 --> 00:19:49,067
<i> Look what we have here.</i>

467
00:19:49,200 --> 00:19:52,433
<i>We have money, we have power,
we have protection.</i>

468
00:19:52,567 --> 00:19:55,167
<i>And what? You just want
to trade that with peace?</i>

469
00:19:55,300 --> 00:19:57,067
<i> Peace is overrated.</i>

470
00:19:57,200 --> 00:20:00,300
<i> This life will kill us.</i>

471
00:20:00,433 --> 00:20:04,467
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

472
00:20:06,900 --> 00:20:08,367
[CREAKING]

473
00:20:08,500 --> 00:20:11,100
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

474
00:20:11,233 --> 00:20:12,967
[CREAKING]

475
00:20:13,100 --> 00:20:15,800
[CAR REVVING]

476
00:20:22,600 --> 00:20:24,533
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [SCREAMS]

477
00:20:24,667 --> 00:20:26,733
[CRASHES]

478
00:20:28,933 --> 00:20:32,567
Ah, Chief, what happened
to Cruz's contact?

479
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:33,667
<i> For the second time,</i>

480
00:20:33,800 --> 00:20:34,967
<i> he didn't show up.</i>

481
00:20:35,100 --> 00:20:38,167
He tried calling
but couldn't reach him.

482
00:20:38,333 --> 00:20:40,600
<i>The caller's location
can't be traced anymore.</i>

483
00:20:40,733 --> 00:20:42,333
<i>Maybe the phone is off.
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]</i>

484
00:20:42,467 --> 00:20:44,400
Maybe that contact
was just messing around.

485
00:20:44,533 --> 00:20:46,500
And the info he gave,

486
00:20:46,633 --> 00:20:48,333
maybe it wasn't true.

487
00:20:48,467 --> 00:20:49,600
<i> I don't think so.</i>

488
00:20:49,733 --> 00:20:52,667
We have a strong feeling
he wasn't lying.

489
00:20:52,800 --> 00:20:54,300
Chief, did Cruz identify

490
00:20:54,433 --> 00:20:56,800
who called the hotline?

491
00:20:56,933 --> 00:20:58,767
<i> Liza De Leon.</i>

492
00:20:58,900 --> 00:21:00,700
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

493
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:08,200
[OSTRICH CLUCKINPG]

494
00:21:11,267 --> 00:21:13,833
[OSTRICH CLUCKINPG]

495
00:21:15,467 --> 00:21:17,100
Good morning, Joey.
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

496
00:21:17,233 --> 00:21:18,633
Good morning.

497
00:21:19,500 --> 00:21:21,100
I wanted to feed them.

498
00:21:21,233 --> 00:21:23,633
But they won't come near.

499
00:21:23,767 --> 00:21:24,767
Ah, them?

500
00:21:24,900 --> 00:21:27,200
[OSTRICH CLUCKINPG]

501
00:21:28,333 --> 00:21:29,833
Okay, I'll help you.

502
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:34,000
Jin Ho!
[CLICKS TONGUE]

503
00:21:34,133 --> 00:21:35,600
Peter!
Come here!

504
00:21:35,733 --> 00:21:38,367
[CLICKS TONGUE]

505
00:21:39,900 --> 00:21:40,833
Jin Ho!

506
00:21:40,967 --> 00:21:43,167
No use, they're stubborn.

507
00:21:44,267 --> 00:21:45,533
I can do it.

508
00:21:46,833 --> 00:21:48,600
Ah, Andrew...

509
00:21:49,033 --> 00:21:52,667
About what I said to you
before...

510
00:21:53,433 --> 00:21:54,867
Forget it, okay?

511
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:57,000
I also thought it's better

512
00:21:57,133 --> 00:21:59,200
